Operator directive 2026-08-07, the FOYSAL leaderboard-technique-watch lever
(2026-08-01 entry, arc-agi3-leaderboard-technique-watch.md): on level-up,
replay the previous level's successful trace re-anchored to the new level by
object matching + mean centroid displacement, before spending an LLM
re-induction call. FOYSAL's own implementation was source-reading and
therefore forbidden; the general-purpose technique underneath it is not.

Three pieces:
- arc_solver_kit.object_relative_trajectory_transfer (new primitive, file
  tail, purely additive): object_centric_digest on both levels' opening
  grids, greedy same-color matching by (area diff, centroid distance),
  ACTION6 clicks translated by the mean displacement scaled by cell, OOB
  clicks dropped (never clamped) via _action6_out_of_live_bounds.
  transfer_confident requires BOTH matched_fraction and displacement_std
  thresholds -- neither alone is sufficient.
- E3AgentPolicy._begin_level_goal_episode stashes the completed level's
  trace (explore transitions + executed plan steps) and opening grid at the
  one instant both are intact -- mirrors the pre-existing win-transition
  capture immediately above it. Defensive getattr (not a hard attribute
  access) after this exact change broke a PRE-EXISTING test that constructs
  the policy with a placeholder object() transition -- caught and fixed
  before it reached CI.
- New cascade stage in _induce_and_plan's level_up_reinduction branch,
  before execute_bounded_llm_reinduction: on a confident transfer, installs
  the plan and returns with engine_source="object_relative_trajectory_transfer",
  byte-identical exit shape to the structured-nav/TTT tiers beside it.

DEFAULT OFF (SUBMITTED_OBJECT_RELATIVE_TRAJECTORY_TRANSFER_ENABLED = False,
env CARNOT_ARC_TRAJECTORY_TRANSFER) pending an A/B -- the lever presumes the
next level is an object-translated variant of the previous one, true for
some ARC games and false for others. Fire-counters recorded on every
outcome (including a distinct no-completed-level-trace case) per the
exp5836 dead-observe-channel discipline. arc_solver_kit imported directly
(function-scoped) so the primitive is genuinely execution-reachable, not
merely lint-closure-reachable; scripts/arc_orphan_solver_lint.py confirmed
green (69 modules).

17 new tests (10 primitive-isolation, 7 cascade-wiring) plus the fixed
pre-existing one, all passing. Broader sweep of every test file that
exercises _begin_level_goal_episode/_observe_level_boundary directly (36
more tests) also passing.

Artifact-freshness: 11 artifacts drifted on arc_competition_agent.py (the
cascade stage is flag-gated dead code when off; the trace-capture runs
unconditionally but is strictly additive -- three new attributes, no
